4069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=i-j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)j \\\\  & =(2x-y)\\,i+(2y-x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(2(1)-1)\\,i+(2(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =∇\\,f(1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(i+j)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(1)+1(-1)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c362cd907fb85830ab3320317ae756b56808309a5fb6a6d98274061b8fc74a3f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Ac