evaluate it at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x+y),\\,6xz⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,0,1) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1+0)+3\\cdot {1}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1+0),\\,6\\cdot 1\\cdot 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+3,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi +3,\\,-1,\\,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $⟨-\\pi +3,\\,-1,\\,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c362cd907fb85830ab3320317ae756b56808309a5fb6a6d98274061b8fc74a3f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jak